%% DM26-0670

%% Runtime attestation, slice A: the instance check at issuance (runtime-attestation.md, "Slice A, the askers"). Built, but for what was signed before it could be attested.
%% At issuance a pod is checked against its owner; the Deployments are checked against the signed record continually (the maintainer, 2026-11-02).
%% The agent's verdicts stand only while it has proved itself (attestation-when-it-cannot-answer.md, "The agent proves itself").
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Init as polar-init (a workload's pod)
    participant Obs as Credentials observer
    participant CA as Credentials agent
    participant Att as Attestation agent
    participant API as Kubernetes API
    participant CI as cert-issuer
    participant Sch as Configuration agent
    participant Repo as Deployment repository, on Polar's git server

    Note over Att,API: read from what it already holds, not a call per question
    Att->>API: watch pods, ReplicaSets, Deployments, StatefulSets and Jobs in Polar's namespaces (get, list, watch only)
    API-->>Att: every change

    loop each minute, when a list finishes, and when a new record arrives
        Att->>Att: prove itself: every watch listed, its own pods genuine, most of what runs not condemned, real pods altered all refused
        Note over Att: Failing: an ERROR, and CannotSay to everything. With no record: pods held to their owners, and verdicts stand that far
    end

    Init->>Obs: issuance request, with the token Kubernetes signed for this pod
    Obs->>CA: the request, over Cassini
    CA->>CA: verify the token, its identity and the pod UID it is bound to (an IdP's credential has no pod, and is not asked about)
    CA->>Att: attestation-instance-requests: this identity, this pod UID (a custodian's as its service's)

    alt the attestation agent answers
        Att->>Att: the pod exists with that UID, and has no ephemeral container
        Att->>Att: its owner chain, by UID, ends at the workload the signed record names for the identity
        Att->>Att: it runs as the expected service account
        Att->>Att: each container's image and imageID (the kubelet's) is the digest its nearest owner pins
        alt all of them hold
            Att-->>CA: Genuine
            CA->>CA: the renewal rule, which records what it admits, so only now
            CA->>CI: vouch for the certificate
            CI-->>CA: signed
            CA-->>Init: the certificate, through the observer
        else any of them does not
            Att-->>CA: NotGenuine, and why
            CA->>CA: record (InstanceRefused) and log the refusal. Its type is not used up
            CA-->>Init: refused: polar-init stops, and the pod restarts in place and asks again
        end
    else no session (at once), no answer within 2 s, or CannotSay
        CA->>CA: the renewal rule
        CA->>CI: vouch for the certificate
        CI-->>CA: signed
        CA->>CA: record it (IssuedUnattested)
        CA-->>Init: the certificate, through the observer
    end

    Note over Init,CI: a token-only request in one of the core's windows (the floor state's entry open, a ticket)
    Init->>CI: a bootstrap identity's request, on its token alone
    CI->>CI: is its entry open, or a ticket its pod's? If held, the credentials agent asks instead, as above
    CI->>Att: attestation-instance-requests
    Att-->>CI: Genuine or NotGenuine: the attestation decides who gets through
    CI-->>Init: signed, or refused, and a ticket given back. Could not ask: signed, and its record entry says so (unattested)

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over CI,Att: DESIGNED: what was signed before anything could attest it, and while the agent was away
    Att->>CI: cert-issuer's record: each entry carries its pod UID, and says if it was unattested
    CI-->>Att: the entries
    Att->>CA: the same for the issuances recorded as IssuedUnattested
    CA-->>Att: the entries
    Att->>Att: attest every running pod they name
    Att-)CA: any that fail: the credentials agent, as body guard, stops renewing
    end

    Note over Att,Repo: the Deployments against the signed record. An issuance waits on none of this
    Repo-->>Sch: a new commit, carrying the deployment's facts as a document the pipeline certificate signed
    Sch-)Att: every 30 s, the document as it is, on a topic of its own. The configuration agent is not trusted
    Att->>Att: verify it to the deployment CA, for this alone, and refuse an older version
    loop each minute
        Att->>Att: every Deployment's and StatefulSet's pins against the document
    end
    Note over Att: a difference that has lasted ten minutes: an ERROR, for now. Acting on it is slice B
